# Targeted Boxplot for a Single Metabolite R Script

This R script generates a boxplot for a single metabolite across selected culture conditions, using technical replicate columns from a metabolomics matrix. Each condition is shown as a boxplot with its own fill color, overlaid with all individual data points as jittered black dots and a thin median bar.

The script reshapes technical replicate columns (`<replicate>.<condition>.<tech_rep>`) to long format, filters to one metabolite by its `name` value, restricts to a user-defined set of conditions, and orders the x-axis with a custom condition sequence.

## Input

- `VaBaMet_matrix.csv` with a `name` column and technical replicate columns matching `##.XX.##` (e.g., `1.LcGv.1`).

## Output

- `MbC_single_metabolites.png` (8×6 in, 300 dpi)
- `MbC_single_metabolites.svg`

## Requirements

R with `tidyverse` and `svglite`.

## Note

Three user-editable settings must be adjusted per run: `target_metabolite` (must match the `name` column exactly), `keep_conditions` (two pre-written variants for Pb vs. Gv coculture comparisons — keep the one you need), and `desired_order` (two variants, same logic). The output filenames are hardcoded for methyl-β-carboline and should be changed for other metabolites. Set the working directory at the top before running.
